  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_c93a4b3d8c1142ecb1c6b19d4c14c085",
      "statement": "The fencing argument in summary: ownership records use conditional writes so two nodes cannot acquire one cell; replicated data carries its fencing epoch in the object key so a deposed node writes only into a superseded prefix; and before acknowledging a write celld proves the write durable and confirms it still owns the cell.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L108-L113",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:74fd443a1d919e35de87e491830992402c3ff668d8452c97b31b6c22a2c081a8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b9b81506cf68433ca44a83d73ea022aa",
      "statement": "The bucket must provide conditional create, conditional overwrite, and read-after-write consistency; the qualified stores are S3, R2, Tigris, GCS, and Azure Blob Storage, a store ignoring or faking conditionals fails late and silently, so the startup probe and celld diagnose check them empirically and a node that finds a broken store stops.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L32-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3b5daadee42156614e73a0e54187d815e094545c837aee269db9762b30925230:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L88-L102",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ec95db4186deedb1df0e373baa4c35e1530ff5bbd4278725fc074e9d66142585:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_91abb590b62e4523a8cb109eaeb2ed53",
      "statement": "Each cell has one ownership record naming the owner node's session and carrying a fencing epoch; acquisition is a conditional write (create if absent, CAS against the previous record otherwise), so the bucket accepts exactly one of two contenders; and every activation advances the epoch so an epoch never has two writers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L110-L120",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a5c13cddc60705767dfbae4f950986de33a58526c7e266e2c0e38b1864c0699d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_02b1bf51801345ff8b040993c151cae3",
      "statement": "The owner record's wire shape is exactly node and epoch with the CAS etag surfaced separately by load_json, and read_owner returns an OwnerRecord carrying node (mapping empty string to deliberately-released ownerless), epoch, and the etag used for subsequent conditional writes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/ownership_store.rs#L20-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:31dbf63db142a8979d396789e6475efbca34077fd8d952e4629579bfe1f5081c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/ownership_store.rs#L287-L301",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c38d25a6038f85d7c36c21bf08da09791f3fdb82ee788f905b00299cb2af0525:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bcb6e38ec4e544b598a5d1fe8a4ab1a8",
      "statement": "RestoreSpec carries exactly the facts ownership resolution decided — epoch, fresh (this activation conditionally created epoch one so no replica can precede it), took_over, resume_local (the node-level lease handoff proved this exact local epoch remains authoritative and the adapter must not consult the remote replica), and prior (the node the takeover displaced, for the node-log takeover interlock) — and the effect adapter must not rediscover or guess these.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L33-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:45e130afc7dfe3a5c8d1fbcf262872756f3ca9de23e32f823d4ede6d68be3e6b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d4c86d44971c46b1a8828e4af6f43b89",
      "statement": "Each node holds a lease in the bucket renewed after one third of its lifetime (CELLD_TTL_MS, default 10000 ms); a renewal that does not reach the bucket does not immediately fence because the node retries while the published expiry has not passed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L202-L212",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e10339150614805f571bd339b49820e78ad9ff5985df7c5e292c928177ce365a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_eff0fe5d47a047b28905780fa2aba7f8",
      "statement": "When the published lease expiry passes — or another writer replaces or removes the lease record — the node fences itself: it stops each active cell and fails every request it has not completed; routing already compares the current time against the published expiry on each request, so a paused node is not routed to even before the fence runs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L213-L214",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2d69630a0b7214497e8423b0fe7bae87a2bcb2f1e8621e0065e1f49316491b21:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3f9cc272f7ab461dafbcb1e18b472c06",
      "statement": "The fence writes nothing to the bucket: peers already read the lease as dead or replaced and acquire cells through the ownership records.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L215-L217",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:beb16cf34450de8d80588582e4bac82a7127918e700e20a30c9b20a226d387a4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b978b47a21fa4ca8b3c1bedff7144ce7",
      "statement": "The fenced-state log line mechanism: a node that self-fences and exits without saying why leaves an operator with an unexplained exit code, so celld deliberately names the fence cause in the log.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main.rs#L237-L242",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:45301ce8d339f4149aba1ba4dc4648f271d2052a7fdb38637f01ede88bda6a10:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7ba19be30e914558a2d9b3b5c92ee34a",
      "statement": "A fenced node logs a line starting with SELF-FENCE: and stops with exit code 3; other internal failures use the same prefix and code; the fenced state is terminal and only a restart returns the node to the fleet through the same cold-activation path a peer failure uses.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L198-L210",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:91dcd5d9e58abd7c14d3408f0de65fc860d7ae7e35e5e76f49be70f3d82b8346:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b1640ad11f714d3c9c960d53d6384455",
      "statement": "The operator must run celld under a supervisor that restarts the process (systemd, Docker restart policy, Kubernetes) with no attempt limit and at least one lease lifetime between attempts, because a fenced process exits and without a restart the fleet loses that capacity.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L62-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:85d3f73595ed611f9dd12c1db3f19a26e77017e51778aa449ba79d258d446c94:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e87472cbb3c64b82bb07664dce7b4aab",
      "statement": "RecoverNodeLog is the takeover interlock at claim time: the dead owner's folded log state was not sealed, so its acked tail may exist only on followers; the executor recovering every non-sealed session of the prior owner into the bucket is a precondition of the claim proceeding.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L769-L776",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eaed267f167de899c5eda37c23b09b055997f176a91885b5bec9952f537aa1b9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_09f9503071d3482b829de50fc64e276c",
      "statement": "Each process session creates a conditional node-log record before its first fleet-durable acknowledgement; a takeover runs recovery (CAS the record, seal reachable followers, upload their retained segments and bundles into per-cell prefixes, then mark sealed) before restoring, so the activation cannot restore mid-recovery.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L158-L175",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:19030f1b45e7fb58ae8498895e1693a9e37db598d115182f0e94bd9ed7e8c2cb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1774d32630784246a0e55bee49737450",
      "statement": "Dead-node reconciliation retry pacing is deterministic core policy: retry_delay_ms(tick_ms, failure_count) computes the backoff, and parse_marker_key identifies node/cell marker object keys.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/dead_node_reconciliation.rs#L15-L26",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ed2b5b82fea147500d7af1ea0bcd45c766e39e179956234d7b4cc643e8d3bca8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fbee9d19c3564f66b6e25f3eaff26e78",
      "statement": "The dead-node record carries the folded node log as the fleet log's root of truth: retirement must respect its state and the tombstone must carry it through unchanged because the record IS the fleet log's durable state in one body.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/dead_node_gc.rs#L27-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3851102185268586329cea3db93ee917860e59ff359e84c7af40ade475e1ddb6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4ce81ce4a28248aab91cc4a8dc023949",
      "statement": "A fenced node appending an unacknowledged tail to an older epoch prefix is not a contract violation: a failed or absent acknowledgement does not prove the write is absent, so restore may expose it; the promise is that acknowledged writes are never lost, not that unacknowledged writes never surface.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L213-L217",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:30f1b1d3c710fbdb9b018fb4254d49811986069bcd9006c9165c052a2e8708d3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ecfe76e017384879a63c44d49764e686",
      "statement": "StopCause::Evict { rebalance } distinguishes two evictions: rebalance=true releases the ownership record and hands the cell to the fleet (the local replica is not worth keeping), while an idle eviction keeps the record and local replica so the next activation on this node renames the file into place instead of paying a full remote restore.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L930-L940",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d8f858d624c3d34d57f9265e7d29686be54517ef67b082d5b874e67bc81d1126:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ae176c76b58c42299e88f7eff499863c",
      "statement": "Memory-pressure shedding policy is decided by the core: classify() latches node load into pressure states and release_target/walk_metric decide when to shed and which cells, so the executor never sheds a cell on its own judgment.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/pressure.rs#L203-L263",
